[100.129988, "i", "\"    error: failure,\\n    incident,\\n  });\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat >> docs/operations.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Failed-job incidents\n\nAfter the final failed attempt, the runner sends an incident to `tracker` (Faultline).\nSuccessful runs do not send incidents. The failed oplog entry records `incident` as\n`sent`, `suppressed`, or `undelivered`; tracker outages do not change the job's exit code.\n\n`var/incidents.json` keeps per-fingerprint occurrence counts, the first failure time, and\nlast successful send time (`null` until delivered). Repeats within\n`incident.dedupe_window_minutes` of the last successful send are counted but suppressed.\nThe window uses the run's `--now` clock, not wall time. Failed deliveries count too, but\nnever advance the last successful send time.\n\nIncidents include the final attempt's last `incident.log_tail_lines` lines and the job's\nsettings. Settings outside the tracker's accepted schema classes are masked; the ledger\nDSN is projected to its scheme/host/port/database, without credentials or "]
